# A program commands the DPMS blank with the Linux console's sequences
# (vtium/vtium#79): setterm times it, and a program wakes the displays
# without a key.
#
#   make vt-check GUIDE=blank

title: a program times and wakes the blank

step: setterm times the blank, and a program wakes it
run: TERM=linux setterm --blank 1; sleep 90; printf '\033[13]'
do: after Enter, touch no key or the pointer until the question below the
do: command comes back.
expect: the screen goes dark about a minute after Enter, and lights again
expect: about half a minute later with no key pressed, this screen drawn
expect: whole, then the question.

step: RIS returns the blank to dpms-timeout
run: printf '\033c'; sleep 90
do: after Enter, touch nothing until the question comes back, a minute and
do: a half later.
expect: RIS clears the screen at once, and it stays lit until the question:
expect: the program's minute has given way to dpms-timeout's 600 seconds.
